In conclusion we have described, for the first time, the heteroepitaxial growth of MOF crystals on a copper hydroxide substrate. A salient aspect of this protocol is that precisely aligned MOF films can be readily fabricated on centimetre length scales. Moreover, we showed how the framework pore channels can orient dye molecules and engender an anisotropic optical response. Due to the fundamental interest and widespread technological importance of materials with anisotropic properties such oriented polycrystalline MOF thin films are poised for further exploration and development.
