## Methods
Synthesis of \(\mathbf{Cu}_{2}(\mathbf{BDC})_{2}\) on copper hydroxide nanotube. Oriented copper hydroxide nanotubes were synthesized from a Cu metallic thin film deposited on a Si wafer. The conversion solution from metal to hydroxide was prepared by mixing \(4\,\mathrm{ml}\) of \(10\,\mathrm{M}\,\mathrm{NaOH}\) aqueous solution, \(2\,\mathrm{ml}\) of \(1\,\mathrm{M}\,(\mathrm{NH}_{4})_{2}\mathrm{S}_{2}\mathrm{O}_{8}\) aqueous solution and \(9\,\mathrm{ml}\) of deionized water. The Cu film deposited on a Si wafer was immersed into the mixed solution for \(15\,\mathrm{min}\) at room temperature. Then, the substrate was collected from the solution and washed with water and ethanol. The copper hydroxide nanotube film on a Si wafer was dried and stored under ambient conditions. The conversion from copper hydroxide to \(\mathrm{Cu}_{2}(\mathrm{BDC})_{2}\) was performed at room temperature by immersing the obtained copper hydroxide nanotube film in a saturated ligand solution \((3.6\,\mathrm{ml}\) of water, \(9.34\,\mathrm{ml}\) of ethanol mixture, \(0.1\,\mathrm{g}\) of \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{BDC})\) . After \(5\,\mathrm{min}\) , the product was removed from the solution and washed with water and ethanol, and then dried under air.
Synthesis of Cu-MOF with different ligands. Cu-MOFs from different ligands were synthesized on oriented \(\mathrm{Cu}(\mathrm{OH})_{2}\) nanobelts films. The oriented \(\mathrm{Cu}(\mathrm{OH})_{2}\)
nanobelt films were immersed into a conversion solution \((3.6\,\mathrm{ml}\) of water, \(9.34\,\mathrm{ml}\) of ethanol mixture, \(0.04\,\mathrm{g}\) of ligands) for different conversion times: \(\mathrm{H}_{2}(2,6\mathrm{-}\mathrm{NDC})\) \((2,6\,\mathrm{naphthalenedicarboxyl}\) acid) \(30\,\mathrm{min}\) , \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{BPDC}\) ( \(4,4^{\prime}\) -biphenyldicarboxylic acid) \(1\,\mathrm{h}\) , \(\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{TPDC}\) ( \(\boldsymbol{p}\) -terphenyl- \(\cdot4,4^{\prime\prime}\) -dicarboxylic acid) \(2\,\mathrm{{h}}\) . In the case of \(\mathrm{H}_{3}\mathrm{BTC}\) ligand, conversion from copper hydroxide to \(\mathrm{Cu}_{3}(\mathrm{BTC})_{2}\) was performed41. The conversion solution was \(1.8\,\mathrm{ml}\) of water, \(4.67\,\mathrm{ml}\) of ethanol and \(0.21\,\mathrm{g}\) of \(\mathrm{H}_{3}\mathrm{BTC}\) .
